# __REPO_NAME__ — your training repo

This is **your** repo for working through your training curriculum. Each session is an
interactive conversation with **Alex**, your AI tutor; the repo handles git, session
branches, and PRs for you automatically. This README is your operating manual — how to
run **this** repo. You never need to know how it was built.

## Where everything goes

All your work lives under **`__TRAINEE__/`**:

| Folder | What goes here |
|---|---|
| `__TRAINEE__/sourceDocs/` | Source & reference material (add anything external here **before** using it) |
| `__TRAINEE__/inputDocs/` | Documents **you** write during a session |
| `__TRAINEE__/outputDocs/` | Summaries & documents Alex produces for you |
| `__TRAINEE__/sessions/` | Per-session records (`__TRAINEE___{date}_session-N/`) |
| `__TRAINEE__/trainee-profile.md` | Who you are + what you want from the course (anchors every example) |
| `__TRAINEE__/training-state.md` | Where you are in the curriculum |
| `__TRAINEE__/feedback.md` · `improvement-recommendations.md` | Alex's running notes |

Nothing you produce should land at the repo **root** — always inside `__TRAINEE__/`.

## Starting a session

1. Clone your repo and run `claude`.
2. Say hello:

   ```text
   Hi Alex, this is {your name}
   ```

That is the whole launch ritual — **no git, no environment variables, no ids to
paste.** Alex reads your brief from the repo (`trainee-brief.md`) and picks up exactly
where your last session left off. This works even fully offline — the briefing lives
in the repo, not on a server.

## What happens automatically

- **At session start** you are moved onto a fresh session branch off `main`, and any
  pending update instruction from the training team (the *operational brief*) is
  surfaced — Alex will explain it and only apply it with your approval.
- **While you work**, if you try to read a document from **outside** this repo you'll
  get a reminder to copy it into `__TRAINEE__/sourceDocs/` first (keeps your context
  contained and reproducible).
- **At session end** (a clean exit) the session log is copied into `logs/`, your work
  is committed and pushed, and a **pull request to `main`** is opened.

## The next-session ritual

Your **next** session starts by reviewing the PR your last session opened: Alex walks
you through the summary, you check the work, and **merge** it. Then carry on. Many
sessions accumulate this way — that's your progress over time.

## First time on this workstation?

The repo needs a little one-time setup with your trainer — filling in
**`training-config.yaml`** (your scoped database key) and optionally `gh` auth. Work
through **`docs/workstation-setup.md`** together, then run
`python3 .claude/hooks/trainee-preflight.py` to confirm everything is ready. The full
list is in `docs/dependency-analysis.md`. Until then the repo stays quiet — sessions
still work fully offline; only progress telemetry and team updates wait for the setup.
